# ---- Application ----
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---- Auth (required at runtime) ----
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-32-byte-random-secret
AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true

# ---- Database ----
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://triyara:triyara@localhost:5432/triyara_bnp

# ---- Storage (supplier and buyer documents) ----
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: "local" writes to the filesystem. Zero-config, works with
# `pnpm dev`, and is the default.
#
# PRODUCTION: "local" is REFUSED. The app will not start with it, on purpose —
# a serverless filesystem is read-only outside /tmp and is discarded between
# invocations, so uploads appear to succeed and the document is gone. Set s3
# or r2 below. See docs/07-deployment/README.md.
STORAGE_PROVIDER=local

# Local only.
# STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR=.storage
# STORAGE_SECRET=change-me-for-signed-local-urls   # falls back to AUTH_SECRET

# ---- Storage: production (REQUIRED when STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3 or r2) ----
# All three of BUCKET, ACCESS_KEY_ID and SECRET_ACCESS_KEY must be set or the
# app refuses to start rather than failing one upload at a time.
# STORAGE_BUCKET=triyara-bnp-documents
# STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#
# AWS S3: set the real region, leave STORAGE_ENDPOINT unset.
# STORAGE_REGION=ap-south-1
#
# Cloudflare R2: region is always "auto" and the endpoint is required.
# STORAGE_REGION=auto
# STORAGE_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com

# ---- Public registration ----
# The tenant public supplier and buyer registrations are filed under. Both
# public forms read this; if the slug does not match a real organization,
# every submission is rejected.
# PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_ORG_SLUG=triyara

# ---- Email (Resend) ----
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: leave RESEND_API_KEY unset. Messages are written to the
# log instead of sent, so nothing leaves the machine and the password-reset
# link is still readable in the console.
#
# PRODUCTION: both RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM are REQUIRED. The app refuses
# to start without them — a supplier or buyer has no account and no inbox in
# the product, so email is the only way they ever hear back, and silently not
# sending is indistinguishable from never having registered.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Must be a domain verified in Resend, or every message is rejected.
# EMAIL_FROM=TRIYARA <noreply@triyaraexports.com>
#
# Where replies from suppliers and buyers should land. Optional but strongly
# recommended: rejection emails invite a reply, and without this they go to a
# noreply address nobody reads.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=sourcing@triyaraexports.com
#
# Comma-separated. Who is told that a new supplier or buyer has registered.
# If unset, nobody is alerted and registrations wait unseen in the queue.
# EMAIL_STAFF_NOTIFICATIONS=ops@triyaraexports.com,swapnil@triyaraexports.com

# ---- Super administrator ----
# Who may approve, reject and revoke admin access requests. ADMIN is never
# assigned directly; this list is the only authority that can grant it, and
# holding ADMIN is NOT sufficient to decide a request.
#
# Comma-separated, so Stage-2 adds people without a code change. If unset it
# falls back to the Stage-1 super administrator, which keeps development and
# the seeded database working — a platform with nobody on this list could
# never grant ADMIN again.
# SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS=swapnilrahate6598@gmail.com

# ---- Application URL ----
# Absolute origin used to build links in emails (password reset, review queue).
# Without it, links fall back to VERCEL_URL and then to localhost — which is
# fine locally and useless in a real reset email.
# APP_URL=https://bnp.triyaraexports.com
